  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">14</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML workflows and frontier-class AI models to reveal causal relationships between material response and experimental/UGT diagnostic data. This is directly about understanding and modeling materials behavior using AI across rich experimental datasets, which aligns most closely with the materials lifecycle and AI-driven materials workflows in “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence.” The WBS under Stockpile Research and Primary Assessment Technologies supports that this is materials/response-focused rather than design-production integration, facility operations, threat response, or historical data digitization. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">36412500.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_17">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">17</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on using machine learning to predict compatibility/incompatibility of energetic materials, which is directly about materials behavior and reliability. Among the challenges, only “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” centers on AI-driven workflows for material design, performance prediction, and qualification. The WBS and STAT context (Aging &amp; Lifetimes, Engineering) further support that this is about ensuring safe, reliable materials performance for the stockpile rather than nonproliferation, data archiving, regulatory streamlining, or acquisition.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">24666363.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_18">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">18</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is simply “Materials Aging &amp; Compatibility,” under the Aging &amp; Lifetimes WBS within Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering. This points to work on understanding and qualifying how materials evolve, degrade, and remain compatible over time in support of the stockpile. Among the Genesis challenges, the one explicitly focused on materials discovery, production, and qualification for deterrence best matches this mission area. There is no indication of nonproliferation monitoring, historical data digitization, enterprise regulatory streamlining, or DA/PA integration, so the materials-focused challenge is the closest fit, though the brief scope text limits certainty.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">29440823.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_30">
