  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">30</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on applying AI/ML techniques for qualification of CT data for part acceptance, which is directly about using AI to support material/component qualification processes. The WBS and STAT context (Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification under Rapid &amp; Advanced Capabilities) further ties this effort to improving certification and qualification workflows for deterrence-related components. Among the candidate challenges, this aligns most closely with “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence,” which explicitly targets AI-enabled, end-to-end material and component qualification and certification, rather than design-production integration, business processes, archival data, or experimental facility operations.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">1750000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_31">
