  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">32</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on materials R&amp;D and qualification: (1) using a large language model to identify replacement high-explosive binder candidates, and (2) developing high‑performance, multi‑metal alloys optimized for strength and stability with new additive manufacturing methods that meet future system requirements. This is directly aligned with accelerating discovery, production, and qualification of mission‑critical materials and leveraging advanced manufacturing, which is the core of the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge. The WBS/STAT context of Advanced Manufacturing Development further supports this mapping over design/production integration, facility capacity, regulatory streamlining, or threat response challenges.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">11537446.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_4">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">4</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is simply “High Z Materials,” and the WBS/STAT context is “Dynamic Materials Properties” under Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering. This points to research on high‑atomic‑number materials and their dynamic properties in support of the stockpile, which aligns most directly with the challenge focused on accelerating materials discovery, production, and qualification for deterrence. Other challenges emphasize nonproliferation monitoring, historical data digitization, regulatory/safety process streamlining, or business processes, none of which are indicated by the brief materials-focused scope. Because the description is terse and does not explicitly mention production or qualification workflows, confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">2500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_5">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">5</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description, “Inverse design of AM lattices,” points to AI-driven materials and structure design for additive manufacturing, which aligns most directly with the materials-focused challenge. Inverse design is a core AI method for discovering and optimizing material/structural architectures, and AM lattices are manufactured components whose properties must be understood and qualified. The supporting STAT/WBS context (Dynamic Materials Properties under Assessment Science) further indicates work on material behavior relevant to stockpile components, matching the end-to-end materials discovery/qualification theme better than design–production integration, facility operations, data digitization, or nuclear forensics.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">1200000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_7">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">7</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is explicitly focused on “New materials discovery for HE,” which directly aligns with the challenge centered on accelerating discovery, production, and qualification of mission-critical materials. The associated WBS and STAT context (Dynamic Materials Properties under Assessment Science) further supports that this work is about developing and characterizing new high-explosive materials, matching the materials-focused Genesis challenge rather than data, nonproliferation, emergency response, or design/production integration topics.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">1000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_19">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">19</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML tools to predict compatibility/incompatibility of energetic materials and to build a data-driven predictive capability using multimodal surveillance and aging data (MS and FTIR). This is directly aligned with AI-accelerated materials understanding and qualification for mission-critical materials, which is the core of the “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence” challenge, rather than nonproliferation monitoring, historical data digitization, regulatory streamlining, or facility throughput.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">47405647.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_20">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">20</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on applying AI/ML to support qualification of CT data for part acceptance and demonstrating digital twin performance with real data. This is directly about AI-enabled qualification workflows and digital twins for components, which aligns with the materials discovery/production/qualification lifecycle. The WBS and STAT context of “Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification” further supports mapping to the challenge centered on accelerating material development, production, and qualification for strategic deterrence rather than broader design–production integration, facility operations, or business processes.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">4166000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_24">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">24</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is simply “f-Electron Materials Project,” which directly emphasizes materials. Among the candidate challenges, the only one explicitly centered on materials development and qualification is “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence.” The supporting STAT/WBS context (Physics and Engineering Models under Advanced Simulation and Computing) is consistent with modeling and simulation of advanced materials, which aligns with AI-accelerated materials workflows described in that challenge. Other challenges focus on facilities, regulatory processes, nonproliferation monitoring, or historical data, which do not match the materials-focused scope. Because the description is brief and lacks detail beyond “materials,” confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">19025000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_26">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">26</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automated defect detection for additively manufactured (AM) structures using AI/ML image interpretation to determine defect sizes and assess feasibility of components for war reserve (WR) applications. This is directly about improving qualification and acceptance of manufactured components via AI-driven inspection, which aligns with the materials/manufacturing lifecycle and qualification focus of “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence.” The WBS and STAT context (Advanced Manufacturing Development, Weapon Technology and Manufacturing Maturation) further support this mapping over design/production integration, facility operations, data archiving, or threat response challenges.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">28300000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_27">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">27</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on synthesizing and characterizing target alloys and using machine learning to discover new alloys, which directly aligns with AI-accelerated materials discovery and qualification. Supporting evidence from STAT/WBS (Weapon Technology and Manufacturing Maturation; Advanced Manufacturing Development) reinforces that this is materials R&amp;D for deterrence, matching the materials discovery and qualification challenge more closely than design/production integration, business processes, threat response, or experimental facility operations.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">2700000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
