<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:harnessing_america_s_historic_nuclear_data_and_r:6cbae10ba9" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_19">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">19</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on AI/ML tools to automatically index, catalog, extract metadata, and search across an increased number of digital repositories. This aligns directly with the challenge centered on digitizing, labeling, and organizing historic nuclear data into searchable, well-governed archives for AI-enabled use. The emphasis on metadata extraction, cataloging, and search is a precise match to the proposed AI digitization-and-reconstruction pipeline and centralized archive in “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research,” whereas the other challenges focus on design/production integration, materials, experiments, or operational streamlining rather than data archiving and discovery.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">77548915.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
