  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on Bayesian Model Calibration with ML surrogate models and explicitly includes JASPER work, which is a high-energy-density experimental facility used to study dynamic material properties. This aligns most directly with the challenge centered on increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities, where AI, surrogates, and advanced modeling are used to optimize experiments and extract more information per shot. The WBS and STAT context (Dynamic Materials Properties under Assessment Science) further support that this is experiment-centric rather than purely materials discovery, design/production integration, or regulatory streamlining.</data>
