  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description, “HEA compositions for extreme environments,” points to research on high-entropy alloy behavior under extreme conditions, which aligns most closely with experimental materials science work at high-consequence facilities. Among the options, this best fits the challenge focused on increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities, as such HEA studies typically rely on specialized experimental platforms and diagnostics. However, the description is very brief and does not explicitly mention facilities, experiments, or data/archives, so the mapping is uncertain.</data>
