  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on LANL few-view radiography and applying machine learning to analyze and interpret weapon physics data, which directly supports experimental diagnostics and analysis for hydrodynamic and subcritical tests. The STAT and WBS context (Assessment Science; Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support) indicate work tied to high-consequence experimental facilities and stockpile stewardship experiments. This aligns best with the challenge centered on increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities through AI-driven analysis and optimization of experimental data, rather than business processes, regulatory streamlining, or historical data digitization. SME correction: Corrected</data>
