  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">11</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automatic calibration of Scorpius using ML and discrepancy learning. Scorpius is a hydrodynamic/subcritical experimental facility, and the STAT/WBS context is “Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support,” indicating work to improve execution and analysis of high‑consequence experiments. This aligns best with the challenge on Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities, which targets AI-driven operating systems, calibration, and data use to optimize limited-capacity experimental facilities, rather than business processes, materials, or historical data digitization.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">750000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_12">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">12</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope describes developing a digital twin and modeling tool for the Scorpius accelerator, integrated into the EPICS control system, combining multiple physics models (accelerator gaps, beam transport, target dynamics, radiography). This directly aligns with the challenge focused on an AI-enabled “facility operating system,” digital twins, and real-time experiment planning and execution at high-consequence experimental facilities. The STAT and WBS context (Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support) further support that this is about enhancing experimental facility capability rather than data archiving, business processes, or emergency response.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">3000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_13">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">13</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on Scorpius, a hydrodynamic/subcritical experimental capability, and on developing a modular, data‑driven, ML-based automatic calibration approach. This directly aligns with the challenge to increase experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities via AI-driven facility operating systems, real-time steering, and data/provenance standards. The STAT/WBS context (Assessment Science; Hydrodynamic &amp; Subcritical Execution Support) further supports that this is about optimizing high-consequence experimental facilities rather than business processes, materials pipelines, or historical data digitization.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">3200000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_14">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">14</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope describes developing a modeling tool and digital twin for the Scorpius accelerator, integrating multiple physics models and data sources (ITS data, PushML for accelerator voltages, beam transport codes, target dynamics, and radiography models) into the EPICS control system. This directly aligns with creating AI-enabled facility digital twins and an AI “facility operating system” to plan, steer, and analyze high-consequence experiments, which is the core of the “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities” challenge. The work is clearly experimental-facility-focused rather than business processes, historic data archiving, or emergency/threat response.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">3000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_15">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">15</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very short: “ML tools using Bayesian analysis and simulation.” This most directly aligns with AI/ML methods for optimizing and interpreting experiments, especially Bayesian analysis and simulation-driven design, which are central to the “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities” challenge (AI facility operating system, real-time steering, multi-fidelity simulation, uncertainty-aware analytics). The WBS/STAT context (Stockpile Research, Assessment Science, Primary Assessment Technologies) also points to experimental and diagnostic work in support of stockpile stewardship rather than production workflows, regulatory streamlining, historic data digitization, or emergency response, reinforcing this mapping.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">1100000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_16">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">16</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on traditional ML for radiograph analysis, Gaussian process models for improved uncertainty quantification, and NLTE atomic opacity model construction, all of which are core stockpile assessment and experimental-analysis tools. These methods directly enhance how data from high-consequence experiments are interpreted and how uncertainty is quantified, aligning best with the challenge to increase experimental capacity and information yield at nuclear research facilities. The WBS/STAT context (Secondary Assessment Technologies under Assessment Science) further supports a link to experimental design, diagnostics, and analysis rather than archival data, production integration, emergency response, or nonproliferation monitoring.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">2500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_17">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">17</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on machine learning for analysis and modeling of data from multiple high energy density (HED) experiments, aiming to develop more refined uncertainty quantification (UQ). This aligns best with improving how experimental data are analyzed to increase the value and efficiency of limited, high-consequence experiments, which is central to the “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities” challenge. The WBS/STAT context (Assessment Science, Secondary Assessment Technologies) further supports a link to experimental campaigns and their analysis rather than to historic data digitization, enterprise business processes, design–production integration, or emergency response operations.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">1500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na11:4d4029855b" target="mstc_challenge:increasing_experimental_capacity_at_nuclear_rese:e9a4a1153b" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_18">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">18</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
