  <data key="d17">The scope description mentions “Light sources – data analysis and forward modeling, image processing,” which indicates AI-enabled analysis and modeling of experimental data, likely from high-energy or x-ray light sources used to study material behavior under dynamic conditions. The WBS and STAT context (Assessment Science, Dynamic Materials Properties) suggest work tied to understanding material responses relevant to nuclear weapons and possibly signatures. Among the challenges, the closest thematic fit is the attribution-focused challenge, which emphasizes multimodal analysis (vision, spectroscopy, morphology, inverse modeling) and forward/inverse modeling of signatures. However, the evidence is sparse and does not explicitly mention forensics or attribution, so the mapping is uncertain, leading to low confidence.</data>
