  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very general: an AI initiative launching 3–4 academic centers focused on AI studies and applications, under an academic strategic alliance. It does not reference design/production integration, historic nuclear data, acquisition, or safety/regulatory processes. As a broad, cross-cutting AI program likely to support enterprise data, tools, and workforce development, it most closely aligns with the business and management challenge, which emphasizes an integrated AI ecosystem, unified data, and workforce AI readiness across national security missions. However, the evidence is weak and non-specific, so confidence is low.</data>
