  <data key="d14">3</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on productionizing AI tools that accelerate weapons design, modeling, and simulation workflows (e.g., CHANDLER federated model, Horizon Shield simulation workflow, CADSAT meshing tool) and deploying secure AI infrastructure on classified networks. This directly aligns with the design–production integration and model-based engineering emphasis of “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which calls for AI-accelerated modeling, simulation, and digital twins to improve weapons design and production efficiency. Other challenges emphasize historical data, experimental facilities, regulatory/safety documentation, or business processes rather than core weapons design and production workflows. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">346644000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
