  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on productionizing AI tools that accelerate weapons design, modeling, and simulation workflows (CHANDLER federated model, Horizon Shield simulation workflow, CADSAT meshing tool) and deploying secure AI infrastructure on classified networks. This directly aligns with the “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence” challenge, which emphasizes AI-accelerated, model-based systems engineering, multiscale physics, digital twins, and secure cross-site data and models to improve weapons design and production. The STAT and WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing; Computational Systems &amp; Software Environment) further support this mapping to design/production integration rather than business processes, historical data, experimental facilities, or regulatory streamlining. SME correction: Corrected</data>
