  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">12</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description only states that this UFR is to support the newly launched NNSA Genesis Mission and the development of AI capabilities for nuclear deterrence, without specifying business processes, acquisition, threat response, or forensics. The STAT/WBS context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering → Assessment Science → Dynamic Materials Properties) and the prior NA-11 UFR title “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence” suggest alignment with core weapons design, assessment, and production activities rather than enterprise business or acquisition functions. Among the candidate challenges, this is most consistent with “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which directly targets AI-enabled capabilities for nuclear deterrence design/production workflows. However, because the description is high-level and non-specific to any single challenge, confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">9127000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
