  <data key="d14">15</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI/ML work across multiple high energy density (HED) experiments focused on analysis and modeling of experimental data to develop more refined approaches. This aligns most closely with the challenge centered on increasing experimental capacity at nuclear research facilities, which focuses on AI-driven optimization of experiments, data analysis, and facility throughput. The WBS and STAT context (Assessment Science, Secondary Assessment Technologies) further support a link to experimental design, analysis, and stewardship-related test campaigns rather than materials development, design–production integration, historic data digitization, or emergency response.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">44130500.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
