  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very high-level and only states that this UFR is for the NNSA Genesis Mission and AI tools for nuclear deterrence, without specifying business processes, acquisition, threat response, or forensics. The WBS and STAT context (Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering; Secondary Assessment Technologies) suggest a technical, deterrence-focused R&amp;D effort more aligned with weapons design, modeling, and production than with enterprise business or acquisition functions. Among the candidate challenges, the one most directly tied to nuclear deterrence mission execution and technical design/production integration is “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” so it is the best fit, though the lack of specific detail in the scope limits confidence.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">56442000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
