<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:18" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_18">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">18</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is simply “Materials Aging &amp; Compatibility,” under the Aging &amp; Lifetimes WBS within Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering. This points to work on understanding and qualifying how materials evolve, degrade, and remain compatible over time in support of the stockpile. Among the Genesis challenges, the one explicitly focused on materials discovery, production, and qualification for deterrence best matches this mission area. There is no indication of nonproliferation monitoring, historical data digitization, enterprise regulatory streamlining, or DA/PA integration, so the materials-focused challenge is the closest fit, though the brief scope text limits certainty.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">29440823.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
