<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:22" target="mstc_challenge:harnessing_america_s_historic_nuclear_data_and_r:6cbae10ba9" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_22">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">22</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope emphasizes (1) characterizing and validating materials to improve computational models and (2) “Curating and Analyzing New and Legacy Flight Test Data to Predict Environments of Future Systems.” The explicit focus on curating and analyzing legacy test data to support future predictions aligns most directly with the challenge centered on digitizing, organizing, and exploiting historic nuclear-related data for ongoing research and decision-making. While materials work could relate to the materials challenge, the prominent role of legacy test data curation and analysis is a closer match to “Harnessing America’s Historic Nuclear Data and Research.”</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">22175000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
