<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:27" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_27">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">27</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very high-level and only states that this UFR is for developing AI tools for nuclear deterrence under the Genesis Mission, without specifying business processes, acquisition, historic data, or emergency response. The WBS and STAT context (Stockpile Research, Inertial Confinement Fusion, HED &amp; Ignition Science for Stockpile Applications) point toward weapons design, stockpile applications, and deterrence rather than enterprise business functions or emergency response. Among the candidate challenges, this aligns most closely with “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which is the only one explicitly centered on nuclear deterrence design/production and stockpile-related mission outcomes. However, because the description does not explicitly mention DA/PA integration, digital twins, or production operations, the mapping is uncertain, so confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">20400000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
