  <data key="d17">The scope description only states "Critical Executable CE UFR: Genesis AI" with no specific functional detail. Supporting context shows it is under Multi-Weapon Systems and Stockpile Operations, which most closely aligns with enterprise-wide design/production integration for deterrence rather than facility experiments, materials R&amp;D, regulatory streamlining, or acquisition. Given the minimal scope detail, this mapping is uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">318269000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na12:a44487f5ca" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_34">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">34</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is extremely terse: “Critical Executable CE UFR: Programmatic AI,” giving no direct indication of experiments, materials, acquisition, or regulatory/safety focus. The WBS and STAT context (Multi-Weapon Systems under Stockpile Management/Operations) suggest a cross-cutting, enterprise-level AI capability supporting multiple weapons systems, which most closely aligns with the enterprise “nuclear security enterprise twin” and model-based integration of design and production described in the Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence challenge. However, because the evidence is minimal and non-specific, confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">165115000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na12:a44487f5ca" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_1">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">1</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very short: “Multi-Weapon Systems AI and Digital Transformation IA.” The STAT and WBS context place this in Stockpile Management → Stockpile Operations → Multi-Weapon Systems, which is closely tied to weapons system design/production rather than business, acquisition, or purely experimental facilities. Among the challenges, the one most aligned with multi-weapon systems AI and digital transformation in a deterrence/production context is “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which explicitly targets AI-enabled, model-based integration of design and production for weapons systems. However, because the description lacks detail and could conceivably map to other AI/digital efforts, confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">18626000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na12:a44487f5ca" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_55">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">55</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is only the word "Validated," providing almost no direct evidence. Supporting context indicates AI-focused digital transformation work under Stockpile Management → Stockpile Operations → Multi-Weapon Systems, which most closely aligns with integrating design and production activities for weapons systems rather than business processes, acquisition, or facility operations. Given the multi-weapon systems focus and AI/digital transformation, the best fit is the challenge centered on an AI-accelerated, model-based platform spanning design and production for nuclear deterrence, but the lack of detailed scope text limits confidence.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">11481000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
