  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">34</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is extremely terse: “Critical Executable CE UFR: Programmatic AI,” giving no direct indication of experiments, materials, acquisition, or regulatory/safety focus. The WBS and STAT context (Multi-Weapon Systems under Stockpile Management/Operations) suggest a cross-cutting, enterprise-level AI capability supporting multiple weapons systems, which most closely aligns with the enterprise “nuclear security enterprise twin” and model-based integration of design and production described in the Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence challenge. However, because the evidence is minimal and non-specific, confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">165115000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
