  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on strengthening international law enforcement, intelligence, and security agencies’ capabilities to detect, disrupt, and investigate nuclear smuggling. This aligns directly with nonproliferation and preventing illicit movement of nuclear materials, which is the core of the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge. The WBS and STAT hierarchy (Global Material Security, Nuclear Smuggling Detection and Deterrence) further support that the mission is about detecting and deterring proliferation-related smuggling rather than emergency response, forensics, enterprise acquisition, or weapons design/production.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">79705000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
