<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:39" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_enterprise_acquisition:5ed1760af3" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_39">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">39</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automation and AI/ML to enhance the e810 system and streamline the process for submitting civil nuclear technology transfer requests under 10 CFR Part 810. This is an acquisition/authorization workflow optimization problem—improving a complex, regulation-driven process for approvals and submissions—matching the Accelerating Nuclear Enterprise Acquisition challenge, which targets AI-enabled, policy-grounded platforms to interpret regulations and automate tasks across acquisition and related compliance lifecycles. The WBS and STAT context in nonproliferation support this interpretation but the core activity is process and system efficiency, not monitoring proliferation, digitizing historic data, or design/production integration.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
