<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:40" target="mstc_challenge:safeguarding_nuclear_materials_from_proliferatio:616a01e1a8" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_40">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">40</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on supporting and implementing activities under EO 14299 and expanding IAEA safeguards at U.S. nuclear facilities, which is directly tied to international safeguards, nonproliferation, and monitoring of nuclear materials. The WBS and STAT lines are for Civil Nuclear Cooperation &amp; Engagement under Nonproliferation and Arms Control (NA-20), reinforcing that the effort is about safeguards and nonproliferation rather than emergency response, acquisition, or experimental capacity. This aligns most closely with the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which centers on enhancing monitoring, detection, and enforcement of nonproliferation commitments. The (CUI) AI-induced proliferation challenge lacks specific safeguards/IAEA context in the provided description, making it a weaker fit than the safeguards-focused challenge.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">20000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
