<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_csv:42" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_csv_42">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">42</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on designing and maintaining major reactor plant components and systems for technologically superior naval nuclear propulsion. This aligns most closely with integrating advanced design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, where AI-enabled, model-based engineering and digital twins support complex nuclear system design, production, and lifecycle maintenance. The WBS and STAT context (Naval Reactors Development, Reactor Systems &amp; Component Technology) further indicate a design/production engineering mission rather than acquisition process optimization, historical data digitization, or emergency response, making the design-and-production-focused Genesis challenge the best fit.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">16200000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA30</data>
</edge>
