  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">45</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes advancing AI tools for rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events, detailed analysis of vast and varied data, and nuclear incident preparedness, which directly aligns with the challenge focused on shrinking detection-to-response times and providing real-time situational awareness for nuclear/radiological events. The WBS and STAT context (Nuclear Incident Preparedness and Collaboration, NA-81) further support an emergency response and threat assessment mission rather than long-term data curation, acquisition reform, nonproliferation monitoring, or pure attribution-only focus. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">5000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA80</data>
</edge>
