  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">59</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on funding annual licenses and tokens for AI capabilities, without specifying nuclear design, production, or materials activities. The program interest area is listed as “AI GENESIS PLATFORM,” and the WBS/STAT context is Information Technology &amp; Cybersecurity, suggesting enterprise IT/AI tooling rather than mission-specific nuclear engineering. Among the candidate challenges, this best aligns with the challenge centered on an integrated AI platform to accelerate business and management processes across national security missions, which would naturally require enterprise AI licenses and platform tokens.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">2500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:naim:e600e447ad" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_business_and_management_processes_f:1739dbeef6" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_62">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">62</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope emphasizes enterprise-wide AI enablement: AI innovation and collaboration, core computing and connectivity, secure AI models and tools, data governance and cybersecurity, and AI readiness workforce training. These are foundational, cross-cutting business and management capabilities rather than mission-specific acquisition, production, or historic data efforts. This aligns directly with the challenge focused on an integrated AI ecosystem, unified business and management platform, and an AI-ready workforce to accelerate planning, programming, budgeting, and other management processes for national security missions.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">636625000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
</edge>
