  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">61</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope describes a mixed-classification high-performance computing resource concept to efficiently support NNSA’s growing mission demand across multiple offices, framed as an AI Genesis platform and categorized under Information Technology &amp; Cybersecurity. This aligns best with the business and management challenge, which emphasizes an integrated AI ecosystem and unified platforms that improve efficiency and support decision-making across enterprise functions, rather than being specific to nuclear threat response, weapons design/production, historic data digitization, or materials R&amp;D. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">45000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:naim:e600e447ad" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_57">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">57</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on funding employee access to core Microsoft and DOE services and tools to enable widespread innovation in day-to-day operations across the enterprise. This is generic enterprise IT that underpins business workflows and collaboration rather than mission-specific acquisition, production, or historic data efforts. Among the challenges, the business and management challenge explicitly targets an integrated AI-enabled ecosystem and unified platforms that improve underlying business and management functions and day-to-day processes, which best matches broad enterprise IT enablement. Other challenges are more narrowly focused on acquisition, design/production, safety/regulatory processes, or historic data digitization, which are not indicated here. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">17682020.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:naim:e600e447ad" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_58">
