  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">58</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes improving DOE fire response capabilities, increasing AI capacity for mission-critical classified work, and specifically benefiting NNSA’s radiological and nuclear emergency response missions, along with deployment of AI infrastructure. Among the options, this aligns most directly with the challenge focused on shrinking detection-to-response times and providing real-time decision support for nuclear and radiological events. The other challenges center on forensics attribution, nonproliferation monitoring, experimental facilities, or acquisition, which are not mentioned in the scope description. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">362324875.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NAIM</data>
</edge>
