<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:1" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_1">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">1</data>
  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very short: “Multi-Weapon Systems AI and Digital Transformation IA.” The STAT and WBS context place this in Stockpile Management → Stockpile Operations → Multi-Weapon Systems, which is closely tied to weapons system design/production rather than business, acquisition, or purely experimental facilities. Among the challenges, the one most aligned with multi-weapon systems AI and digital transformation in a deterrence/production context is “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which explicitly targets AI-enabled, model-based integration of design and production for weapons systems. However, because the description lacks detail and could conceivably map to other AI/digital efforts, confidence is low.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">18626000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA12</data>
</edge>
