  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is very short: “ML tools using Bayesian analysis and simulation.” This most directly aligns with AI/ML methods for optimizing and interpreting experiments, especially Bayesian analysis and simulation-driven design, which are central to the “Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities” challenge (AI facility operating system, real-time steering, multi-fidelity simulation, uncertainty-aware analytics). The WBS/STAT context (Stockpile Research, Assessment Science, Primary Assessment Technologies) also points to experimental and diagnostic work in support of stockpile stewardship rather than production workflows, regulatory streamlining, historic data digitization, or emergency response, reinforcing this mapping.</data>
