  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description focuses on nuclear reactions on unstable isotopes and surrogate reactions at TAMU, which are experimental nuclear physics activities. Among the challenges, this aligns best with Increasing Experimental Capacity at Nuclear Research Facilities, which targets optimizing experiments and facility use. The match is indirect because the description does not explicitly mention AI, facilities, or data systems, but the experimental nature and STAT/WBS context under Assessment Science and Secondary Assessment Technologies suggest support to experimental campaigns rather than design/production integration, historical data digitization, emergency response, or business processes.</data>
