<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:26" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_materials_discovery_production_and:e89fa227cf" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_26">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">26</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automated defect detection for additively manufactured (AM) structures using AI/ML image interpretation to determine defect sizes and assess feasibility of components for war reserve (WR) applications. This is directly about improving qualification and acceptance of manufactured components via AI-driven inspection, which aligns with the materials/manufacturing lifecycle and qualification focus of “Accelerating Materials Discovery, Production, and Qualification for Strategic Deterrence.” The WBS and STAT context (Advanced Manufacturing Development, Weapon Technology and Manufacturing Maturation) further support this mapping over design/production integration, facility operations, data archiving, or threat response challenges.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">28300000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
