<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:30" target="mstc_challenge:strengthening_deterrence_through_attribution_of:12318fe125" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_30">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">30</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on developing technologies to detect and characterize foreign nuclear weapons programs and to monitor, characterize, and interdict nuclear materials outside regulatory control. This aligns directly with nonproliferation monitoring, anomaly detection, and safeguarding nuclear materials from rogue actors, which is the core of the “Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats” challenge. Supporting evidence includes STAT lines under Defense Nuclear Nonproliferation R&amp;D and Proliferation Detection, reinforcing the nonproliferation detection mission rather than emergency response, acquisition, or deterrence production. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">165000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
