  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is extremely sparse, only stating it is the NSM portion for “Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence.” This clearly links to nuclear deterrence and AI, but does not specify design/production, emergency response, nonproliferation monitoring, or experimental facilities. The STAT/WBS context (Assessment Science, Primary Assessment Technologies) suggests work related to assessing or characterizing nuclear devices or materials, which aligns somewhat better with nuclear forensics and attribution than with design/production integration, broad threat-response fusion, nonproliferation monitoring, or facility operations. Because the evidence is weak and largely generic, the mapping to “Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures” is tentative, so confidence is low. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">25831000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
