  <data key="d17">The scope description and program request both emphasize developing AI tools specifically for nuclear deterrence, without mentioning production, facilities, or forensics. The WBS/STAT context is “Primary Assessment Technologies” under “Assessment Science,” indicating a focus on assessing nuclear threats and supporting deterrence decisions. Among the challenges, this aligns best with “Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response,” which centers on AI-enabled assessment and decision support for nuclear and radiological events, rather than design/production integration, experimental facility optimization, or detailed forensic attribution. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
