  <data key="d17">The scope description and program request only state "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence" with no further detail. This clearly links to nuclear deterrence but does not specify forensics, emergency response, nonproliferation monitoring, or experimental facilities, making those challenges less directly supported. Among the deterrence-focused options, the most generic fit is the design/production deterrence challenge, which explicitly targets AI-enabled capabilities for nuclear deterrence, though the evidence is sparse and nonspecific, so confidence is low. SME correction: Corrected</data>
