  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description and program request both emphasize developing AI tools specifically for nuclear deterrence, without mentioning production, facilities, or emergency response operations. The WBS and STAT context (Assessment Science, Secondary Assessment Technologies) point toward analytical and forensic capabilities related to assessing nuclear devices and materials rather than design/production integration or facility throughput. Among the challenges, strengthening deterrence through attribution of nuclear and radiological signatures most closely aligns with AI-enabled assessment and characterization work that underpins deterrence by enabling attribution, matching the assessment-focused WBS and deterrence framing in the title. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">30224000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
