<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:41" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_41">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">41</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is “Production Simulation and Digital Twins,” which directly aligns with the Integrating Design and Production Operations challenge’s focus on an AI-powered “nuclear security enterprise twin” and production digital twins to co-optimize design and manufacturing. Supporting evidence from the WBS (Advanced Certification &amp; Qualification) and STAT (Rapid &amp; Advanced Capabilities under Stockpile Research, Technology, and Engineering) further indicates work at the design–production interface for stockpile systems, matching this challenge more closely than materials-focused, regulatory, experimental-capacity, or historical-data challenges.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">12500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
