  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data, and reduce costs across Defense Programs. This aligns most directly with the challenge focused on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, which centers on AI-accelerated, model-based engineering to speed modernization and improve efficiency. The program request title, “DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE,” and the STAT/WBS context under Advanced Simulation and Computing further support a focus on design and production modernization rather than emergency response, forensics, regulatory streamlining, or archival data digitization.</data>
