  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data, and reduce costs through efficiency across Defense Programs. This aligns most directly with the challenge focused on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, which centers on AI-accelerated, model-based systems engineering to speed design/production iterations and improve efficiency. The STAT/WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing; Computational Systems &amp; Software Environment) and the program request for AI tools for nuclear deterrence further support a broad, enterprise-level design/production modernization focus rather than data archival, regulatory/safety automation, forensics, or experimental facility throughput specifically.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">506751000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
