  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data, and reduce costs across Defense Programs. This aligns most closely with the challenge focused on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, which centers on AI-accelerated, model-based engineering to speed modernization and improve efficiency. The STAT/WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing, Integrated Codes) and the program request (“DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE”) further support a focus on AI-enabled design and production integration rather than archival data, regulatory streamlining, forensics, or experimental facility operations.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">54157000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
