  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI to revolutionize activities across Defense Programs with accelerated design cycles, better analysis of complex data, and reduced costs through improved efficiency. Among the challenges, this most closely aligns with “Integrating Design and Production Operations for Nuclear Deterrence,” which focuses on AI-accelerated, model-based systems engineering to integrate design and production, improve efficiency, and shorten cycles. The program request explicitly mentions AI tools for nuclear deterrence, and the STAT/WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing; Verification and Validation) supports an AI/modeling focus consistent with this design–production integration challenge rather than data digitization, regulatory streamlining, forensics, or experimental facility operations. However, because the description is broad and not explicitly about DA/PA handoff, confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">52972000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
