<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:53" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_53">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">53</data>
  <data key="d15">medium</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes AI investments to accelerate design cycles, improve analysis of complex data, and reduce costs across Defense Programs. This aligns best with the challenge focused on integrating design and production operations for nuclear deterrence, which centers on AI-accelerated, model-based engineering to speed design/production iterations and improve efficiency. The STAT/WBS context (Advanced Simulation and Computing; Verification and Validation) and the program request (“DEVELOPING ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE TOOLS FOR NUCLEAR DETERRENCE”) further support a design/production and modeling focus rather than data digitization, regulatory streamlining, forensics, or experimental facility operations. However, the description is broad and could touch multiple challenges, so confidence is medium rather than high.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">15642000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
