<edge source="programming_record:programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv:54" target="mstc_challenge:integrating_design_and_production_operations_for:a1b61701e5" id="classified_as_challenge:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_54">
  <data key="d11">classified_as_challenge</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">54</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description is “Production Simulation and Digital Twins,” and the program request is “STOCKPILE PRODUCTION SCIENCE” under Weapon Technology and Manufacturing Maturation. Among the options, the Integrating Design and Production Operations challenge explicitly focuses on an AI-powered “nuclear security enterprise twin,” production digital twins, and co-optimizing design and manufacturing. This aligns directly with production-focused simulation and digital twin work, whereas the other challenges emphasize materials discovery, regulatory/safety documentation, historical data digitization, or experimental facility throughput rather than enterprise production digital twins.</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">100900000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
