  <data key="d15">low</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description and program request only state "Developing Artificial Intelligence Tools for Nuclear Deterrence" with no further detail. This clearly links to deterrence but does not specify whether the AI is for design/production, forensics/attribution, emergency response, acquisition, or facility operations. The WBS (ICF Diagnostics &amp; Instrumentation) suggests work related to diagnostics and experimental support for stockpile research, which could plausibly connect to several challenges. Among the candidate challenges, the one most explicitly centered on deterrence effects of AI tools in an operational nuclear security context is "Strengthening Deterrence Through Attribution of Nuclear and Radiological Signatures," but this mapping is weak because the evidence is too generic. Therefore that challenge is selected with low confidence. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">ROT</data>
  <data key="d19">2365000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA11</data>
</edge>
