<edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:streamlining_production_removing_red_tape_and_en:5c22e0a6a3" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_38">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">38</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes accelerating AI for challenging proliferation detection scenarios, including AI-driven process modeling and AI-enabled system-of-systems digital twins, directly aligned with nonproliferation monitoring and detection. The STAT lines and program request explicitly reference Proliferation Detection under Defense Nuclear Nonproliferation R&amp;D, matching the Safeguarding Nuclear Materials from Proliferation Threats challenge, which focuses on AI-enabled analysis of diverse data to detect proliferation-relevant anomalies. Other challenges (e.g., nuclear data digitization, business processes, emergency response) do not center on foreign proliferation detection, making this mapping highly consistent. SME correction: Corrected</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">342000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na20:3f63a5531c" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_enterprise_acquisition:5ed1760af3" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_39">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">39</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on automation and AI/ML to enhance the e810 system and streamline the process for submitting civil nuclear technology transfer requests under 10 CFR Part 810. This is an acquisition/authorization workflow optimization problem—improving a complex, regulation-driven process for approvals and submissions—matching the Accelerating Nuclear Enterprise Acquisition challenge, which targets AI-enabled, policy-grounded platforms to interpret regulations and automate tasks across acquisition and related compliance lifecycles. The WBS and STAT context in nonproliferation support this interpretation but the core activity is process and system efficiency, not monitoring proliferation, digitizing historic data, or design/production integration.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA20</data>
</edge>
