<edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_47">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">47</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes “surge support for advancing AI-tools for rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events that require detailed analysis of vast and varied data,” which closely matches the problem statement and proposed solution of the Accelerating Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response challenge (rapid response to nuclear/radiological events, multimodal data fusion, real-time decision support). While the scope also mentions improving nuclear forensics analyses, the primary focus is on event response and risk mitigation, aligning more strongly with this challenge than with the attribution-focused deterrence challenge.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">17500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA80</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_csv_48">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">48</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">True</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope description emphasizes advancing AI tools for rapid and effective response to nuclear and radiological events, requiring detailed analysis of vast and varied data—language that closely matches the problem statement for the Nuclear Threat Assessment, Preparedness, and Response challenge. While it also mentions improving the speed and accuracy of nuclear forensics (which aligns with the attribution challenge) and mitigating sensitive information in the public domain, the primary focus and framing are on event response and situational assessment for NEST/incident response missions (NA-84), making the threat assessment and response challenge the best overall fit.</data>
  <data key="d18">UFR</data>
  <data key="d19">87500000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA80</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:accelerating_nuclear_threat_assessment_preparedn:b962e35516" id="funds_challenge_evidence:programming_record_programming_data_fynsp27_wide_csv_31">
  <data key="d11">funds_challenge_evidence</data>
  <data key="d12">1</data>
  <data key="d13">classification_pipeline</data>
  <data key="d14">31</data>
  <data key="d15">high</data>
  <data key="d16">False</data>
  <data key="d17">The scope focuses on analyzing nuclear materials and device designs to advise and enable an effective U.S. Government response to the potential use of a nuclear threat device. This is centered on threat assessment and operational response to nuclear incidents, aligning directly with the mission of accelerating nuclear threat assessment, preparedness, and response. The WBS and STAT context (Nuclear Counterterrorism and Incident Response, Nuclear Threat Science) further support this as an incident-response and threat-assessment activity rather than long-term nonproliferation monitoring, acquisition efficiency, or pure forensic attribution after an event.</data>
  <data key="d18">BASELINE</data>
  <data key="d19">75000000.0</data>
  <data key="d20">NA80</data>
</edge>
<edge source="sub_office:na80:b7721cf532" target="mstc_challenge:cui_preventing_ai_induced_nuclear_proliferation:bbeffc2cf1" id="leads_challenge">
